WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
No Buddhist scripture mentions IVF.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.400
Or gene editing.

3
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.400
Or intensive farming.

4
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.670
Yet Buddhists answer these questions
differently from country to country.

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.920
In Japan, abortion is legal and common,
and temples hold mizuko kuyo rites to

6
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.840
remember the lost child.

7
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.570
Bhutan abolished the
death penalty in 2004.

8
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.910
Thailand, also largely Buddhist, keeps it.

9
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.650
So can five precepts,
taught 2,500 years ago,

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.180
guide choices about IVF,
euthanasia or GM crops?

11
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.330
In this mission, you'll build a
Buddhist toolkit and test it on life,

12
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.990
death and animals.

13
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.490
Then you'll see where Buddhists disagree,

14
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.880
from a murderer at the
door to same-sex marriage.

15
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:51.200
Your mission: find out whether five ancient
precepts can guide choices about modern

16
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.040
issues.
